  "id": "interpersonal-theory",
  "term": "interpersonal theory",
  "definition": "In this packet, interpersonal theory refers to the Interpersonal Theory of Suicide, which explains suicidal desire as arising from thwarted belongingness and perceived burdensomeness, with hopelessness examined as part of this pathway. It highlights how feeling disconnected, unaccepted, or like a burden in relationships can increase suicide risk.",
